    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d481">

                <pb facs="0501" n="329" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg329"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/6958</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Costa Rica</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">San José</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-09-22T08:00:00-05:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 22, 1917, 8 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 1.45 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>By Executive decree issued late last night, published to-day, diplomatic
                    relations with Germany are severed. Germans are promised continued freedom
                    during good behavior. German Chargé d’Affaires to remain here until passports
                    secured for him.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
